# Workflow

This repo is shared by two machines. Never commit or push straight to `main` or `dev`.

## Branches

| Machine | Push only to |
|---|---|
| Tim's MacBook Pro | `tims-macbook-pro` |
| Jordan's MacBook Pro | `jordans-macbook-pro` |

Promotion path:

`tims-macbook-pro` or `jordans-macbook-pro` → `dev` (collaborate) → `main` (go live)

## Agent rules

- If this clone is on `main` or `dev`, switch to the machine branch for this computer before making changes.
- Create commits only on the machine branch.
- `git push` must update the machine branch, never `origin/main` or `origin/dev`.
- After pushing, open or update a pull request into `dev`. Do not merge it unless the user asks.
- Going live is a separate pull request: `dev` → `main`. Never treat a machine-branch push as production.
- Do not force-push `dev` or `main`. Do not fast-forward local `main` with unreviewed machine-branch work.

## This computer

Tim's MacBook Pro: work on `tims-macbook-pro`. Jordan uses `jordans-macbook-pro` on his machine.
